---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { firm } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy and POPIA notice | Mudau Makondelele Attorneys"
  description="How Mudau Makondelele Attorneys collects, uses and protects personal information under the Protection of Personal Information Act."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy and POPIA notice"
    lede="How we collect, use and protect your personal information under the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA)."
    crumbs={[]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated: October 2026</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {firm.name} (registration number {firm.registration}) is the responsible party for personal information
        collected through this website and in the course of our legal practice. Our Information Officer is the
        Director, {firm.director}.
      </p>
      <p>
        {firm.address.lines.join(', ')}. Email <a href={`mailto:${firm.email}`}>{firm.email}</a>,
        telephone <a href={firm.phones[0].href}>{firm.phones[0].label}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Details you give us through the contact form, by phone, WhatsApp or email: your name, contact details and a description of your matter.</li>
        <li>Information needed to act for you once you instruct us, including identity documents required under the Financial Intelligence Centre Act.</li>
        <li>Information about other people involved in your matter, where it is needed to give you legal services.</li>
        <li>Basic technical information our web host records automatically, such as IP address and browser type, used to keep the website secure.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This website does not use advertising or tracking cookies. We may count visits with Cloudflare Web
        Analytics, which does not use cookies or identify individual visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and arrange a consultation.</li>
        <li>To give you legal advice and represent you.</li>
        <li>To meet our legal obligations, including those under the Legal Practice Act, the Financial Intelligence Centre Act and tax law.</li>
        <li>To bill for our services and manage our trust account.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information or use it for marketing without your consent.</p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Only where needed for your matter or required by law: courts and tribunals, advocates and experts we brief
        with your permission, opposing parties' legal representatives, regulators, and service providers who
        support our practice (such as our IT and backup providers) under confidentiality obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Confidentiality and security</h2>
      <p>
        Communications with us about your legal matter are confidential and may be protected by legal professional
        privilege. We keep paper files secured at our offices and electronic files on access-controlled systems
        with regular off-site backups.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become matters are deleted within 12 months. Client files are kept for as long as
        the law and our professional rules require after the matter closes, then destroyed securely.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You may ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>confirm whether we hold personal information about you and give you a copy;</li>
        <li>correct or delete information that is inaccurate, out of date or no longer needed;</li>
        <li>stop processing your information, where the law allows.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Send requests to <a href={`mailto:${firm.email}`}>{firm.email}</a>. Some information may have to be kept,
        for example where the law requires it or where it is privileged.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Please raise any concern with us first so we can put it right. You may also complain to the Information
        Regulator: <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener" target="_blank">inforegulator.org.za</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Access to information (PAIA)</h2>
      <p>Our manual under the Promotion of Access to Information Act is available on request.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 46rem; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  .prose p, .prose ul { margin-top: 0.9rem; }
  .prose ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .updated { color: var(--graphite); font-size: var(--step--1); margin-top: 0 !important; }
</style>
